        "comments": "The assembly drMyrSibi1.hap1.1 is based on 157x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Ancient Environmental Genomics Initiative for Sustainability (AEGIS,\nhttps://globe.ku.dk/research/ancient-environmental-genomics-initiative-for-sustainability). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order an orientation of the contigs located in the centromeric regions (chromosome 1 15.9-24.1 Mbp, chromosome 2 17.6-22.4 Mbp, chromosome 3 15.7-23.5, chromosome 4 17.2-24.5 Mbp, chromosome 5 18.0-24.7 Mbp, chromosome 6 17.2-20.2 Mbp and chromosome 7 7.2-13.0 Mbp) is unknown.",
